From: REIMU A/B <reimu@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] reimu_dbus: property sets wait for the reply

dbus_connection_send() only queues the message, and the callers exit right
after it: server_uid on/off returned 0 and did nothing most of the time (the
LED group stayed as it was). Wait for the reply, which also reports errors.

---
--- a/reimu_dbus.c
+++ b/reimu_dbus.c
@@ -49,9 +49,14 @@
         return !dbus_message_append_args(reimu_dbus_msg, DBUS_TYPE_STRING, &string1, DBUS_TYPE_STRING, &string2, DBUS_TYPE_INVALID);
 }
 
+static int reimu_get_dbus_reply(void);
+
 static int reimu_send_dbus_request(void)
 {
-    return !dbus_connection_send(reimu_dbus_conn, reimu_dbus_msg, NULL);
+    /* with the reply: only queued, the message is lost when the process exits
+     * (server_uid off did nothing, most times), and an error is seen */
+    reimu_get_dbus_reply();
+    return reimu_dbus_reply == NULL;
 }
 
 static int reimu_get_dbus_reply(void)
